Z||000000||RossT||10-13-1999||01:08 AM||||	<BR>I am thinking of joining FOCOA. Has anyone recently joined? If so, how long did it take to get your first isssue?  There has been some concern in the past that this takes several months.  Also has anyone ordered the fiero owner back issue set for $65.00? How long did it take and are you happy?<P>thanks,  Ross||||reg||1
Z||000001||rcn491||10-14-1999||01:14 AM||||The current issues are sent out 4 times a year but they are usually a little late.<BR>I ordered the back issues along with some parts and I got them in about 10 days.<BR>They are interesting and helpful.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RICK||10-14-1999||09:31 AM||||RCN..How many back issue's did you receive?||||reg||5
Z||000003||Carrolles||10-14-1999||06:17 PM||||I joined in July 1997 and ordered the back isues.  They arrived within a week.  I got every issue although some of the very early issues were xerox copies.  The first few issues are more like newsletters than magazines but I loved reading them from the start of issue number one to the end.  It was interesting watching the evolution of the Fiero.<BR>There are many technical topics throughout the issues with an index somewhere along the way.  I xerox the technical articles and keep them in a folder for use in the garage.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||10-14-1999||09:05 PM||||Thanks guys, I think that I will order the<BR>back issues. BTW how far back to they go?<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000005||rcn491||10-15-1999||01:18 AM||||They sent all the issues from the start of the organization. The first ones are more of a newsletter, 4 or 5 pages. The magazines start in 1986.||||reg||1
